This policy establishes guidelines for employee business expenses.

Rules:
1. Meals: All meal expenses must be under $50 per person.
2. Alcohol: Alcohol expenses are strictly prohibited and will be rejected.
3. Travel: Flights must be booked in Economy class. Business class is reserved for executive staff only.
4. Taxis: Ride-sharing services and taxis are permitted only if a cheaper public transit route is unavailable.
5. Client Entertainment: Must have a pre-approved budget limit and specify all attendees.

If any expense exceeds these limits, it will be flagged for manual review.
If an expense violates a strict prohibition, it will be automatically rejected.